Hex digits in percent-encoding ignore case, but the package turned only the uppercase forms of a
truncated `%C2` and the UTF-16 byte order marks `%FE%FF` and `%FF%FE` into replacement characters
(U+FFFD): `%c2`, `%fe%ff`, `%Fe%fF` and so on were kept as is. Now both checks compare the text in
upper case. It's safe because `decode` only gets runs of ASCII `%XX` sequences. The latest release
(0.5.1) still has this bug.

